        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>How much of the band the Iridium scanner covers. Iridium assigns a duplex channel when a call is set up, out of about 240 across 7 MHz, so watching a single channel sees only a few percent of the traffic. The whole width is split into channels and a receiver run on each, which costs proportionally more CPU. There is no point choosing a width the device cannot supply.</string>
