        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Aero link quality, averaged over the last few seconds. EVM is the RMS error vector magnitude of the coherent detector, from the in-phase component only - the quadrature axis of an MSK symbol carries the other arm's crosstalk and says nothing about signal quality. SU is the fraction of signal units whose CRC passes, which is what actually decides whether a message can be reassembled: a ten unit message needs every one of them</string>
